    // flows", its Bingham case). Under the yield stress it is an elastic solid and keeps its shape; over it, it flows
    // as a thick liquid and comes to rest again when the stress falls. The stress is kappa/2 (J^2 - 1) I for its
    // volume and mu dev(b) for its shape (their equation 2), b the left Cauchy-Green tensor with its volume taken
    // out. When the shape's stress s is over sqrt(2/3) of the yield stress it is brought back by their equation 17,
    // s - (s - sqrt(2/3) yield) / (1 + viscosity / (2 mu~ dt)), and b with it (equation 18): its direction stands.
    let e = eigen(transpose(F) * F);
    let sig = sqrt(max(e.d, vec3f(1e-8)));
    let U = F * e.v * mat3x3f(1.0 / sig.x, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 / sig.y, 0.0, 0.0, 0.0, 1.0 / sig.z);
    let J = max(sig.x * sig.y * sig.z, 0.05);
