    // yields far sooner and flows more easily: a clay's yield stress and viscosity fall off exponentially with the
    // water in it. Here to 8% and 14% when it has taken all it can, where it runs nearly as water does and is carried
    // off; The rates and those ends are this page's, from no paper. (Its taking up is exchange.js's.)
    // So a block in a pool goes soft from the outside in, and what goes soft is washed away.
    //
    // Lava (material 8) is the same fluid with other numbers. Molten, it yields at almost nothing and is very thick
    // (a slow, sticky flow); as it cools (exchange.js keeps how molten it is, 0 to 1, where mud keeps its soaking) its
