  // Li et al. 2026's measure for the powder a moving snowpack throws up, which the exchange takes it by: exchange.js.)
  // (And sand's, which the exchange takes by a coefficient of its own, pressed or pulled: a strike drives a bed
  // together, and pulling apart alone, a ball fired into dry sand threw up 9 particles' worth of dust.)
  // (Sand only once it moves at over 50 cells a second, 1.5 m/s: a cone at rest, its grains stirring a little under
  // the heap's great pressure, gave a thousand particles to the air and slumped from 24 degrees to 16; and at 0.6 m/s
